jessica_sales: Anne (DeltaSurge) - streaming demo failing: client JSON errors mid-stream.
anne_customer: Android WebView; parser shows Unexpected end of input. attaching short HAR: https://files.example/ds-har-05.zip
paul_dev: reproduced locally on Android webview. partial 'data:' blocks arrive then next frame continues. parser tries to parse each arrival.
omar_se: can you confirm any edge proxy or rewrites?
anne_customer: internal edge proxy only, no CDN.
liam_infra: quick grep shows recent change to buffered writer (2026-02-18) toggles autoFlush after N tokens. could cause flush between event lines.
kate_e2e: we previously had a bug where writer.flush() ran before writing final "\n\n". if that happens clients that parse incrementally will see truncated JSON.
nick_support: mitigation plan: 1) client-side buffering until full SSE event (\n\n) - minimal effort; 2) infra rollback of auto-flush optimizer; 3) offer Dedicated trial to avoid proxied paths.
omar_se: I'll prepare an SDK wrapper patch for webview that buffers and reassembles SSE messages. snippet below:```js
let buffer = '';
resp.on('data', chunk => {
  buffer += chunk;
  let idx;
  while ((idx = buffer.indexOf('\n\n')) !== -1) {
    const ev = buffer.slice(0, idx);
    buffer = buffer.slice(idx + 2);
    const data = ev.split('\n').filter(l => l.startsWith('data:')).map(l => l.replace(/^data:\s*/, '')).join('');
    try { handle(JSON.parse(data)); } catch(e) { console.warn('partial json, rebuffer', e); buffer = ev + '\n\n' + buffer; break; }
  }
});
```
liam_infra: I'll revert the optimizer and add logs: SSE_WRITE(id=%s len=%d flushed=%b). also recommend proxy_buffering off if nginx.
deploy-bot: deploy queued: staging/runtime-revert requested by @liam_infra - ETA 15m
nick_support: Anne, can your dev Paul apply the SDK patch tomorrow? we can also send a prebuilt artifact.
anne_customer: Paul will try the patch AM PST. thanks.
jessica_sales: I'll send Dedicated trial info + short-term elevated quota while we triage. also they asked about private deployment options for compliance.
kate_e2e: will add e2e test to simulate split frames and ensure client reassembly works.
paul_dev: will validate and report. if SDK patch works we may avoid infra rollback.
liam_infra: long-term: ensure producer always emits trailing blank line per SSE spec and add unit tests for chunk boundaries.
nick_support: follow-ups: @omar_se SDK PR, @liam_infra revert + logs, @jessica_sales pricing/quote, customer to test client patch. :thumbsup:
